<Base title="About | murmurgrove">
  <section class="about-simple" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <h1 id="about-heading" class="sr-only">About</h1>
    <p>murmurgrove is an evolving research archive shaped by encounters with contemporary art, the questions that follow, and the relationships that continue to emerge.</p>
    <p>Exhibitions, Institutions, People, and Concepts are different ways into the same body of records. The organism on the homepage makes some of these changing relationships perceptible, without claiming to represent everything the archive knows.</p>
    <p>The research moves between curatorial practices, site-specific and public art, and the institutions through which art circulates and takes on meaning. Notes may appear in Chinese, Japanese, or English. The archive remains situated, selective, and open to revision.</p>
    <p>Records are documents of particular encounters, not neutral or exhaustive histories. Connections may be refined as new evidence becomes available. The past is not rewritten to make the present look more certain.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
